7d6189d6 (1568 1793444455287 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f409") (src . "context: hard blocks shown below full are named in insufficient\n\nWhen the budget did not hold a hard block in full, the upgrade pass left\nit at summary or at identity and the answer said nothing: the target\nitself could arrive as a summary with no mark that it had been cut, and\na reader took the answer for the whole block. Only a hard block left out\naltogether was named, in insufficient's missing list.\n\nThe insufficient clause now has a second list:\n\n    (insufficient [(reduced ((<id> <level> (full <bytes>)) ...)\n                            [(more <n>)] [(capped)])]\n                  [(missing ((<id> <bytes>) ...))]\n                  [(more <n> (bytes <b>))])\n\nreduced names every hard block shown below full, the target first and\nthe rest in hard order, with the level it is shown at and the wire\nlength its entry would have at full, as the upgrade pass measured it.\nTwenty are named and the rest counted in the list's own more; a figure\nabove 999999 is shown at 999999 and the list then says (capped), as the\nexcluded counters do. The clause is absent exactly when every hard block\nis shown in full.\n\nThe envelope reserves the list at its largest, from the request and the\nhard set alone: min(20, hard blocks) items of the longest hard id at\nidentity with a six-digit figure, the more only when there are more than\ntwenty hard blocks, separately from the missing reservation, which is\nunchanged. The insufficient wrapper is reserved whenever there is a hard\nblock. The minimum budget of a one-block request grows by the clause\nholding one item, about twenty tokens.\n\nREADME: the budget paragraph says the reservation, where reduced is\nproduced in the steps, its shape and its cap.\n\nTests: context-verb gains CT-reduced-1..6 on three stores (the target\nalone with a large text; the target and three members, one short; the\ntarget and twenty-five large members): the target at summary and at\nidentity named with its length at full and nothing missing; the target\nin full and two members below full named in hard order without the\ntarget; more than twenty below full at the smallest budget that shows\nevery hard block, twenty named and the rest counted, the answer within\nits budget; the minimum grown by one item and min+0 answering ok; and\nthe control with room, every block full and no clause. All but the\ncontrol red on the base. Dropping the reservation fails five rows:\nCT-reduced-5, CT-reduced-6 and three C4 rows. Rows whose exact clause\nchanged: two C4 rows now meet a clause with reduced and no missing, and\ntheir helper reads an absent missing list as none, their text unchanged;\ncontext-users U9's minimum is 452, from 432. The context-verb and\ncontext-users rows-baseline lines move. No row exercises the capped\nbranch.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 567))))
